# Cursor Rules for Get Part B Optimizer (mypartb)

You are an expert AI assistant configured to work on **Get Part B Optimizer** (project: `mypartb`), a high-performance web application built with **React 19**, **TanStack Start**, **Vite**, **Tailwind CSS v4**, and **Supabase**.

Always adhere to the following architectural, design, styling, and testing rules.

---

## 1. Project Overview & Domain Constraints
- **Purpose**: Medicare plan evaluation and agent management console. Side-by-side comparison of Original Medicare + Medigap vs. Medicare Advantage modeling.
- **Zero-PII Model**: The application is built strictly around a de-identified scenario model. 
  - **NEVER** collect, store, or solicit Personally Identifiable Information (PII) such as full name, full address, full date of birth, phone number, email (unless agent login), Social Security Number, or Medicare ID.
  - scenarios must only require a **year of birth** and a **3-digit ZIP code (ZIP3)**.
  - Scenarios are accessed via a generated/temporary **Scenario ID**.
  - All data decays/auto-deletes after 90 days.

---

## 2. Tech Stack & Directory Layout
- **Frontend/SSR**: React 19, Vite, TanStack Start compiling on the Nitro engine.
- **Routing**: TanStack Router (`@tanstack/react-router`) with file-based routing.
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 + Radix UI primitives.
- **Database/Auth**: Supabase client integration.
- **Runtime & Scripts**: Bun (`bun run dev`, `bun run test`, `bun run e2e`).

### Directory Structure
- `src/routes/`: Route declarations. Every route file uses `createFileRoute("/path")` and includes SEO metadata in its `head` definition.
- `src/components/`: Shared React components.
- `src/components/ui/`: Presentation/UI primitives (shadcn-style, Radix).
- `src/lib/`: Business logic, medicare calculations (`medicare-math.ts`), export formats (PDF/Excel), and API functions.
- `src/integrations/supabase/`: Client and server connections to Supabase.
- `e2e/`: Playwright E2E test suites.
- `src/**/__tests__/`: Vitest unit/integration tests co-located with their code.

---

## 3. Code & Styling Standards

### Tailwind CSS v4 (CSS-First Configuration)
- The project uses **Tailwind CSS v4**. Do not look for `tailwind.config.js`. 
- Custom styles, color tokens, and animation definitions are declared in `src/styles.css` using the `@theme inline` directive.
- All colors must use `oklch()` format (e.g. `oklch(0.27 0.11 280)`).
- Respect light/dark modes using `:root` and `.dark` variables in `src/styles.css`.
- Use the `.glass` class for glassmorphism styling, `.grad-indigo` for main brand gradients, and `.script` for script font.

### Supabase Queries
- **Client Side**: Import the default client using:
  ```typescript
  import { supabase } from "@/integrations/supabase/client";
  ```
- **Server Side / Server Functions**: Use the admin client to bypass Row Level Security (RLS) for server-side trusted processes only:
  ```typescript
  import { supabaseAdmin } from "@/integrations/supabase/client.server";
  ```
- Ensure all tables queried map to types in `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`.

### Routing (TanStack Start/Router)
- When adding a route, define it under `src/routes/`.
- Always set the page title and meta description in the route's `head` function to follow SEO best practices:
  ```typescript
  export const Route = createFileRoute('/my-path')({
    head: () => ({
      meta: [
        { title: "Page Title — Get Part B Optimizer" },
        { name: "description", content: "Compelling description..." }
      ],
    }),
    component: MyComponent
  });
  ```

---

## 4. Testing Policy (Strict & Mandatory)
Every change or new feature **MUST** ship with automated tests in the same PR.

### Decision Matrix for Tests
| Kind of change | Required coverage |
| :--- | :--- |
| Pure logic / utility / validator / formula | Vitest unit test under `src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts(x)` |
| Reducer, hook, store, permission gate, data transform | Vitest unit test (mock IO with `vi.mock`) |
| Security gate (uploads, role checks, signature verification) | Vitest test for the happy path **and** each reject path |
| New public route (auth gating, redirect, title) | Add a case to `e2e/smoke.spec.ts` |
| New user-facing flow (form submit, multi-step wizard, modal) | Playwright spec under `e2e/*.spec.ts` |
| Server function (`createServerFn`) | Vitest test for the handler + auth/validation paths |
| Pre-existing edge function change | `supabase--test_edge_functions` Deno test |
| Pure UI restyle with no behavior change | No new test required |

### Test Commands
- **Unit Tests**: Run `bun run test` (Vitest).
- **E2E Tests**: Run `bun run e2e` (Playwright).
- Do **not** weaken tests to make them pass — fix the code or update the assertions properly.
